# Campaign Slides — Product Story First

Applies to every product gallery / carousel campaign (the 12 slides under `public/images/<x>_campaign/`
or `<x>_art/`, CapCut or Seedance plates, EN/RU/AR).

## The job: a product story that sticks

We are not being creative for its own sake. Each campaign tells **the product's story** so it sticks
in the buyer's memory. Creative works together with marketing; creative for taste alone is a failure.

- One through-line per product, said in one line, that carries a real benefit. Product 69 "For your
  eyes only." works: it is made for the eye area *and* it is personal. Product 49 "Five lights. One
  dome." works: every slide teaches one light.
- Every slide must make the buyer understand the product better. If a metaphor needs explaining or
  could belong to any product, it fails. Product 41 "Covered." (multi-tool, keys, wax seal, pocket
  watch) was criticised as "not about the cushion at all".
- When a metaphor would confuse, show the product doing its job instead (compact and puff, a swatch of
  the formula). Clarity beats cleverness.
- It is business, not play.

## Hard rules

1. **Clean hero.** The main image (the product card on the site and in the app) is a clean packshot on
   white. Never add props, splashes, light shafts, type or scenery to it: "it is a product card, it
   must be clean". No exceptions: product 53 lost its gel drops on 2 Oct 2026.
   **Carton or not:** a single-item product (one serum, one cream, one tube pair) shows the product
   alone, no carton: it is what the buyer uses, it reads bigger in the grid tile, and the range lines up.
   The carton goes in the gallery (closing card). A set, kit, refill pack or multi-vial box shows the
   box with its contents, because the box is what the buyer receives (41 cushion + refill, 60 vials,
   beauty boxes). Decided 1 Oct 2026 on product 18.
2. **Never show needles or instruments to buyers.** No sewing needles, pins, syringes, scalpels,
   calipers, microscopes, multi-tools, knives, lab gear, and no macro shots of microneedles. A
   microneedling product is shown whole, never its needles in close-up.
3. **No marketplace lifestyle shots.** No woman in a towel, no spa bed, no stock "person using the
   product" scene: it kills the premium chain. People only when the metaphor needs them, framed as art.
4. **No Dubai images.** No skyline, Burj Khalifa, towers, streets, traffic, malls, office lobbies, heat
   haze. Heat, sun, AC or Gulf context goes in the words, never in a location photo.
5. **Do not redo a live campaign unless asked.** Fix the weak slides; do not replace a set that works.

## Style (product 39 and product 69 are the reference sets)

- **Two colours only**: the pack colour + one concept colour, alternating seamless backgrounds.
- **One visual metaphor per slide**, shot as a minimal studio still. Not stock lifestyle.
- **Witty headline in two levels**, caps, then one short support line with the real fact.
- **Giant numerals** for real doses.
- **Product appears late** (final one or two slides) unless showing it is what makes the story clear.
- **Real packs stay real**: on pack slides composite the real cut-out packs onto the plate, or re-shoot
  a reference, so labels are never garbled.
- Type: Manrope **Regular**, caps headline ~140 px on 2560, leading 0.92; support 64 px sentence case;
  pack colour on the light colour, light colour on the pack colour. Final card lists the product and
  credentials and ends SHOP GENOSYS.AE / GENOSYS UAE APP.

Claims follow `selling-tone.mdc` and the product's source audit.
